Hi Bernardo,

As you suggest, you have a lot of options.  Venn diagrams can be useful for a quick survey of overlapping group memberships, especially if (as in your case) you have no more than three groups.  Google "R cran venn" and you will see a few.

Your choice of technique should be guided by the scope and depth of the analysis you wish to perform.   Here at Bioconductor, we tend to think that the analysis of experimental data is a nuanced and ongoing process, in which early stage explorations often lead to questions and analyses not obvious at first blush.  R is a great language for exploring data, and may be worthwhile for you to learn: point-and-click analysis tools will take you only so far.

If you could give us a better idea of what you hope to learn from your analysis, we can probably give you more specific advice.

 - Paul


  

